  <h2>Safe and Sustainable Dyeing</h2>
  <p>For activewear that sits close to the skin, the safety of the dyes used is paramount. International standards like Oeko-Tex and GRS provide the framework for ensuring product safety and environmental responsibility.</p>
  
  <h3>Oeko-Tex Standard 100</h3>
  <p>This is one of the world's best-known labels for textiles tested for harmful substances. It stands for customer confidence and high product safety. If your leggings are Oeko-Tex certified, it means every component, from thread to finish, has been tested for over 100 harmful chemicals.</p>

  <h3>GRS (Global Recycled Standard)</h3>
  <p>The GRS is an international, voluntary, full product standard that sets requirements for third-party certification of recycled content, chain of custody, social and environmental practices, and chemical restrictions.</p>

  <h3>Our Dyeing Process</h3>
  <p>At Fitclo, we partner with certified dye houses that utilize low-impact dyes and water-recycling systems. This not only ensures the safety of the wearer but also significantly reduces the toxic runoff associated with traditional textile manufacturing.</p>
